ID: vr-16
Title: Deferred custom avatar feasibility and identity gate
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/15

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: An evidence-backed go/no-go decision for a custom animated identity.
Dependencies: None

Purpose:
The owner parked the supplied static model for later, while retaining the
intention to implement it in future. This is a DEFERRED plan, not permission
to begin modeling, install tools, upload assets or replace the current avatar.
Resume only when the owner explicitly reopens this direction. Resolve rights,
desired likeness and a viable deformation route before expensive asset work.

Tasks:
[ ] 16.1 On resumption, re-identify the exact candidate by private hash/receipt;
    preserve the original and use an ignored, versioned working copy.
[ ] 16.2 Verify modification, runtime use and redistribution rights separately
    for geometry, textures, tooling and motion assets; record unresolved terms.
[ ] 16.3 Inventory local AMD/CPU-compatible modeling and rigging tools. Propose
    pinned additions before any install/download; no paid/cloud assumption.
[ ] 16.4 Establish stable-use versus development lanes, source/profile/cache/
    output ownership and shared CPU/GPU limits before experiments.
[ ] 16.5 Review neutral front, both profiles and three-quarter views with the
    owner. Record desired facial proportions, hair, eye/lip placement and
    explicit identity approval/rejections; images are not calibrated anatomy.
[ ] 16.6 Inspect mouth/eye interiors, facial edge flow, self-intersections,
    thin hair surfaces, symmetry and separability beyond edge-manifold checks.
    Record coordinates, transforms and intended scale without guessing units.
[ ] 16.7 Compare bounded local deformation/retopology and speech-retarget routes.
    Claire displacement vectors must not be assigned to arbitrary vertices.
[ ] 16.8 Run a disposable jaw/lip/lid deformation feasibility slice, or retain
    a specific failure receipt. Check rest recovery, lip closure, eyelid
    coverage and hair/skin separation without claiming natural articulation.
[ ] 16.9 Record the selected route, asset contract, risks, fallback and go/no-go.
    Define candidate acceptance views and comparable performance conditions.

Acceptance criteria:
The owner has explicitly resumed work. Rights and identity decisions are
recorded, not inferred from file possession or a passing test. Feasibility
concludes with an honest go or no-go and evidence; a completed investigation
is not an animation-ready avatar. vr-17 requires a positive go decision and
resolved prerequisites; a no-go leaves downstream work blocked, not successful.
No automatic device activation, external upload, global install or publication.
Current Claire defaults and stable-use runtime remain untouched.

Completion evidence:
Planning only; implementation NOT STARTED and deliberately deferred.
Existing read-only candidate inspection found 239092 vertices/479436 triangles
in one connected mesh, without rig, morphs, UVs, textures or materials. Six
actual static views were inspected locally. Numerical edge/area checks do not
prove facial topology, usable interiors, likeness, riggability or 60fps.
That inspection is baseline evidence, not completion of the tasks above.
Private asset paths, receipts and previews are excluded from issue/book output.

Completion log:
2026-11-19 - Owner parks model implementation and asks for detailed future TODOs,
repository issues and Project updates. Planned only; no model/runtime changes.
